Job Title: Digital Planning Lead
Company: WPP Media South Africa
Location: Johannesburg, South Africa
Reports To: Digital Strategy Lead

Role Overview
The Head of Digital Planning is responsible for translating brand and performance strategies into integrated, full-funnel digital plans that drive measurable business outcomes.
This role sits at the centre of the digital ecosystem, orchestrating investment, channel roles, and timing across brand and performance to ensure a cohesive, effective, and commercially optimised approach.

They are the custodian of:
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Budget allocation&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Channel integration&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Full-funnel design&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Planning principles and governance&nbsp;

Core Role in the Structure
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Not the originator of strategy&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Not the executor of channels&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;But the owner of how strategy comes to life in-market&nbsp;

Key Responsibilities
1. Full-Funnel Planning &amp; Integration
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Develop integrated digital plans spanning:&nbsp;
o &nbsp; &nbsp;Upper funnel (awareness &amp; reach)&nbsp;
o &nbsp; &nbsp;Mid funnel (engagement &amp; consideration)&nbsp;
o &nbsp; &nbsp;Lower funnel (conversion &amp; retention)&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Define the role of each channel within the funnel&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ensure seamless connection between brand-building and performance activity&nbsp;

2. Investment Strategy &amp; Budget Allocation
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Own digital budget allocation across channels and objectives&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Balance investment between demand creation (brand) and demand capture (performance)&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Continuously optimise investment based on performance and learning&nbsp;

3. Channel Orchestration
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ensure all channels work together as a system, not in silos&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Define how search, social, display, eCommerce, and content interact&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Align timing, sequencing, and weight of activity across channels&nbsp;

4. Planning Principles &amp; Governance
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Establish and enforce clear planning frameworks and principles&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Standardise ways of working across teams&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ensure consistency in approach across clients and portfolio&nbsp;

5. Data-Informed Planning
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Use data and insights from both brand and performance teams to inform planning decisions&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Incorporate learnings from test-and-learn programmes into future plans&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Partner with analytics teams to refine planning effectiveness&nbsp;

6. Collaboration Across Leadership Roles
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Work closely with:&nbsp;
o &nbsp; &nbsp;Integrated Head of Strategy (big idea &amp; ATL direction)&nbsp;
o &nbsp; &nbsp;Digital Strategy Lead (brand &amp; social ecosystem)&nbsp;
o &nbsp; &nbsp;Performance Strategy Lead (conversion &amp; optimisation)&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Translate all inputs into a single, unified plan&nbsp;

7. Commercial Accountability
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Ensure plans are aligned to client business outcomes&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Track effectiveness of media investment&nbsp;
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Identify opportunities to drive incremental growth&nbsp;

Key Skills &amp; Experience
• &nbsp; &nbsp;Strong experience in digital/media planning across full funnel&nbsp;

